    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0709" n="605" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg605"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.00/883: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Finley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-20T11:00:00-05:00">June 20, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 12:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>82. Department’s circular June 17, 6 p.m. My impression is that the Panaman
                    Government and public regard the question of recognition of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">de facto</hi> Salvadoran government with indifference.
                    Press has contained only brief notice and no editorial comment regarding
                    manifesto.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Finley</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
